1-\nAparna Popat VedIndependent Director15.421-\nNamita GuptaIndependent Director15.421-\nSanjeev Bikhchandani\n3\nNon-Executive and \nNominee Director\n---\nSutapa BanerjeeIndependent Director15.421-\nDeepinder Goyal\n4\nNon-Executive Director---\nKMP(s)\nDeepinder Goyal\n4\nManaging Director & \nChief Executive Officer\n-00\nAlbinder Singh Dhindsa\n5\nChief Executive Officer -00\nAkshant Goyal\n6\nChief Financial Officer-00\nSandhya SethiaCompany Secretary & \nCompliance Officer\n16.021.04    9.34\nThe percentage increase in the median remuneration of employees in the financial year\n7\nThe overall median remuneration of employees has increased by 27.25% (on standalone basis) and 25.83% \n(on consolidated basis) as on March 31, 2026.\nThe number of permanent employees on the rolls of Company\n8\nPermanent employees on the rolls of the Company as on March 31, 2026 were 6,750 (on standalone basis) and \n21,995 (on consolidated basis).\n83\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: Board Report\nCompany Overview\n\nAverage percentile increase already made in the salaries of employees other than the managerial personnel \nin the last financial year and its comparison with the percentile increase in the managerial remuneration and \njustification thereof and point out if there are any exceptional circumstances for increase in the managerial \nremuneration\n7\nThe average salaries of employees other than managerial personnel increased by 28.98% (on standalone \nbasis) and 11.14% (on consolidated basis).\nDisclosure with respect to increase in managerial remuneration and justification thereof is not applicable \nas Deepinder Goyal had voluntarily waived his salary for the period from April 1, 2021 until the date of his \nresignation as Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer.\nAffirmation that the remuneration is as per the NRC policy of the Company\nIt is hereby affirmed that the remuneration paid is as per the NRC Policy of the Company. \nNotes:\n1\nExcludes sitting fees paid to the independent directors during the financial year 2025-26. Please refer to page no. 173 for the details \nof sitting fees.\n2\nExcludes the perquisite value of stock options granted in previous years but exercised during the financial year by the employees of \nthe Company.\n3\nThe Company has not paid any remuneration and sitting fees to the Nominee Director of the Company.\n4\nDeepinder Goyal resigned as Director, Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer of the Company effective from the close of business \nhours on February 1, 2026. During his tenure as Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer, he had voluntarily waived his salary. \nSubsequently, he has been appointed as Vice Chairman & Non-Executive Director of the Company effective from March 13, 2026, and \nhe does not draw remuneration and sitting fees in the said capacity.\n5\nAlbinder Singh Dhindsa has voluntarily waived his salary from February 1, 2026.\n6\nAkshant Goyal has voluntarily waived his salary from January 1, 2022.\n7\nIncrease in mean and median salaries as on the end of the financial year, is reflection of ongoing automation and workforce optimization \nall throughout the year. More and more routine, lower-complexity roles were automated or restructured & the workforce shifted towards \nmore skilled and experienced employees.\n8\nPermanent employees include only full- time employees on the payroll of the Company or its subsidiaries. \nFor and on behalf of the Board\nEternal Limited (Formerly known as Zomato Limited)\nSd/-\n    \n    \nSd\n/-\nKaushik Dutta\n      Deepinder Goyal\nChairman & Independent Director Vice Chairman & Non- Executive Director\nDIN: 03328890  DIN: 02613583\nDate: July 22, 2026 Date: July 22, 2026\nPlace: New Delhi\n Pl\nace: New Delhi\n84\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: Board Report\nCompany Overview\n\n85\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: BRSR\nCompany Overview\nSECTION A – GENERAL DISCLOSURES\nI.  Details of the listed entity\n1.Corporate Identity Number (CIN) of the Listed \nEntity\nL93030DL2010PLC198141\n2.Name of the Listed EntityEternal Limited \n3.Year of incorporation2010\n4. Registered office address Ground Floor 12A, 94 Meghdoot Nehru Place, New \nDelhi-110019\n5.Corporate addressPioneer Square Building, Sector 62, Golf Course \nExtension Road, Gurugram, Haryana, 122098\n6.E-mail \ncompanysecretary@eternal.com\n7.Telephone0124-4268565\n8.Website\nwww.eternal.com\n9.Financial year for which reporting is being \ndone\n1\nst\n April 2025 - 31\nst\n March 2026\n10.Name of the Stock Exchange(s) where shares \nare listed \n1. BSE Limited\n2. National Stock Exchange of India Limited (NSE)\n11.Paid-up capitalINR 9,65,03,50,647\n12.Name and contact details (telephone, email \naddress) of the person who may be contacted \nin case of any queries on the BRSR Report\nMs. Anjalli Ravi Kumar\nEmail: companysecretary@eternal.com\nPh: 0124-4268565  \n13.Reporting boundaryStandalone basis*\n14. Name of the assurance providerDeloitte Haskins & Sells LLP \n15. Type of assurance obtainedReasonable and Limited**\n*Eternal Limited (formerly known as Zomato Limited) on a standalone basis includes Eternal Limited’s India operations, Eternal Limited’s \nbranches in Dubai and Abu Dhabi and Foodiebay ESOP Trust (ESOP Trust does not have any operations or employees). \n**Reasonable and Limited assurance of BRSR indicators (Reasonable assurance: BRSR core & select indicators; Limited assurance: \nselect indicators). Please refer to pages 153 to 160 for the assurance report. \nII.  Products/ Services\n16.  Details of business activities (accounting for 90% of the turnover): \nS. No.   Description of Main Activity  Description of Business Activity% of turnover  \nof the entity \n1   Information Service Activities \n(NIC Code: 63999)\nOther information & communication\nservice activities\n100%\n17.  Products/ Services sold by the entity (accounting for 90% of the entity’s turnover): \nS. No.Product/ ServiceNIC Code % of total turnover \ncontributed\n1   India Food Ordering and Delivery Business6399993%*                                           \n *The remaining 7% of the total turnover pertains to revenue generated from other services, classified under NIC Code 63999.\nBusiness Responsibility and Sustainability Report\n\n86\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: BRSR\nCompany Overview\nIII.  Operations\n18.  Number of locations where plants and/ or operations/ offices of the entity are situated: \nLocation\nNumber of plantsNumber of officesȣTotal \nNational 044\nInternational  000\n  *Eternal Limited (formerly known as Zomato Limited), on a standalone basis, has employees working out of 4 directly leased offices \nas on 31\nst\n March 2026 which is reflected in the table above. In addition, our employees work out of 48 co-working spaces in India \nand the UAE. We also have 14 single seater non-operational offices with no employees. The reporting boundary for all financial, \nsocial and governance disclosures in this report, unless otherwise stated, includes all types of offices.\n  Ou\nr environmental disclosures are based on the principles of operational control. These disclosures have been apportioned and \nextrapolated based on data availability, and are further discussed topic-wise as below:\n \n Energy: Our disclosures include energy from fuel used in owned vehicles, Diesel Generator (DG) sets and purchased electricity for \ndirectly leased offices where we have established operational control. Energy from electricity consumed across our offices outside \nour operational control is placed within our value chain and will be taken into account in our value chain disclosures.\n \n Greenhouse Gas (GHG) emissions: Our Scope 1 GHG emissions are limited to those generated by refilling of gas in owned ACs \nand fire extinguishers, fuel used in owned vehicles and directly leased DG sets. Emissions from electricity consumption in directly \nleased offices where we have established operational control are reported in Scope 2 of GHG emissions.\n \n Water: Our boundary for water withdrawal, consumption and discharge is restricted to directly leased offices where we have \nestablished operational control, following the principle of operational control in accordance with Carbon Disclosure Project (CDP) \nand GHG Protocol guidance.\n \n Waste: The reporting boundary for our waste disclosures includes directly leased offices where we have established operational \ncontrol and procured waste management services ourselves.\n These environmental disclosures have been apportioned and extrapolated based on data availability.\n Details on the inclusions within above topics are mentioned under Section C, Principle 6 of this report.\n19.  Markets served by the entity: \n Eternal Limited (formerly known as Zomato Limited) on a standalone basis operates in India and the UAE.\n a.  Number of locationsȣ\nLocationsNumber\nNational (No. of States)  35 (28 States and 7 Union Territories)\nInternational (No. of Countries)  1 (UAE)\n    *The data reported is as on 31\nst\n March 2026.   \n b.  What is the contribution of exports as a percentage of the total turnover of the entity?\n     There is a limited export for Eternal Limited’s (formerly known as Zomato Limited) IP to its overseas \ngroup entities and marketing services to a third party. Total export is 0.02% of the total revenue from \noperations of Eternal Limited for FY26. \n c.  A brief on typ\nes of customersȣ \n    Fo\nr the purpose of this BRSR disclosure, we have three types of customers as defined below:\n    1.  \n \nEn\nd-users  of  our  platforms- End-users are customers who use our platforms to search and \ndiscover restaurants, read and share reviews, view and upload photos, order food, book a table, \ndiscover and transact across going out experiences. \n  2\n. \n      R\nestaurant  partners- We provide restaurant partners with industry-specific technological tools \nwhich enable them to engage and acquire customers to grow their business while also providing \na reliable and efficient last-mile delivery service.\n  3\n. \n  B\nusiness  partners- These include other partners onboarded on our platform to engage and \nacquire customers. We also provide business partners technological tools that enable customer \ndiscovery, participation in going-out experiences by offering curated offers and discounts and \nto manage certain parts of their business operations.\n\n87\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: BRSR\nCompany Overview\n  Note: As per the Indian Accounting Standards, end-users and delivery partners are considered as Eternal’s \ncustomers only under limited circumstances. For the purpose of this BRSR disclosure, the definition \nof customers includes end-users, restaurant and business partners while delivery partners have been \nconsidered as value chain partners. \n    These customers interact with us via our Zomato Food Ordering and Delivery app, Zomato Dining Partner \napp, Zomato Restaurant Partner app, District app and other business dashboards/ websites.\n *This does not include intercompany transactions.\nIV.  Employees\n20. Details as at the end of Financial Year: \n a. Employees and workers (including differently abled): \nS. No. ParticularsTotal \n(A) \nMaleFemaleOther\nNo. (B) % (B/A) No. (C) % (C/A) No. (D) % (D/A) \nEMPLOYEES\n1.    Permanent (E) 6,750  4,76170.53%1,98729.44%2  0.03%\n2.    Other than permanent \n(F)\n245203   82.86%   4217.14%00%\n3.  Total employees (E + F)6,995  4,96470.96%2,02929.01% 2  0.03%\nWORKERS\n4.    Permanent (G)*0    00%00%00%\n5.    Other than permanent \n(H)** \n544451   82.90%93  17.10%00%\n6.  Total workers (G + H) 544451  82.90%93  17.10%0    0%\n Note: Delivery partners are value chain partners and hence, they are not part of Eternal’s workforce.\n *E\nternal does not engage permanent workers. Hence, details sought for ‘Permanent workers’ category are ‘0’ throughout this report.\n **Other than permanen