business hours on February 1, 2026. Further, while he has been appointed as Vice Chairman & Non-Executive Director \nof the Company, he is not a member of the committee.\n Number of meetings held and attendance of the members\nDuring the financial year under review, no meeting of the committee was held.\nParticulars of senior management personnel including the changes therein\n Particulars of senior management personnel as on the date of report:\nName of employeeDesignation\nAlbinder Singh DhindsaCEO - Eternal\nFounder & CEO - Blinkit \nAkshant GoyalChief Financial Officer\nAditya ManglaCEO - Food Ordering and Delivery Business\nRishi AroraCEO - Hyperpure\nDamini BhallaGeneral Counsel\nSandhya SethiaCompany Secretary and Compliance Officer\nKunal SwarupHead - Corporate Development\nDeepak AhluwaliaGlobal Head - Governance, Risk & Compliance and Internal Auditor\nAli Kausar SiddiquiGlobal Controller - Finance\nAnjalli Ravi KumarChief Sustainability Officer\n\n Changes \nin the senior management personnel since the close of the previous financial year till the date \nof report:\nName of employee DesignationChangeEffective date\nRinshul ChandraCOO - Food Ordering and Delivery BusinessCessationApril 7, 2025\nAditya ManglaCEO - Food Ordering and Delivery BusinessAppointmentJuly 6, 2025\nRakesh RanjanCEO - Food Ordering and Delivery BusinessCessationJuly 6, 2025\n172\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: CGR\nCompany Overview\n\n4. Remuneration to directors\nAll  pecuniary  relationship  or  transactions  of  the  non-executive  directors  vis-à-vis  \nthe Company:\nDuring the financial year under review, apart from payment of annual remuneration and sitting fees, there was \nno pecuniary relationship or transaction with independent directors of the Company.\nAlso, Sanjeev Bikhchandani, Nominee Director of the Company & Deepinder Goyal, Vice Chairman &  \nNon-Executive Director (effective March 13, 2026)  are not entitled to any remuneration and sitting fees.\nCriteria of making payments to non-executive directors:\nThe criteria of making payments to non-executive directors are disclosed under the NRC Policy available at \nLink.\nDisclosure with respect to remuneration:\nDuring the financial year under review, the annual remuneration payable to a single non-executive director \ndid not exceed fifty per cent of the total annual remuneration payable to all the non-executive directors of the \nCompany. Details of remunerations paid/ payable for the financial year:\n(INR crore)\nName of director Fixed annual remunerationSitting fees\nAparna Popat Ved\n1\n1.00.10\nKaushik Dutta\n1\n1.00.19\nNamita Gupta\n1\n1.00.21\nSutapa Banerjee\n1\n1.00.13\nDeepinder Goyal\n2\n--\nSanjeev Bikhchandani\n3\n--\n1\nThe shareholders of the Company vide special resolution dated August 28, 2024 and subsequently vide special resolutions dated March \n13, 2026, approved remuneration of INR 1,00,00,000/- (Indian rupees one crore only) per annum to be paid/payable to each independent \ndirector of the Company.\n2\nDeepinder Goyal resigned as Director, Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer of the Company effective from the close of business \nhours on February 1, 2026. During his tenure as Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer, he had voluntarily waived his salary. \nSubsequently, he has been appointed as Vice Chairman & Non-Executive Director of the Company effective from March 13, 2026, and \nhe does not draw remuneration and sitting fees in the said capacity. \n3\nThe Company did not pay any amount as remuneration and sitting fees to Sanjeev Bikhchandani, Nominee Director.\n5. General Body Meetings\nDetails of last three annual general meetings of the Company held are given under:\nDateTime (IST)Whether special \nresolution passed\nDeemed Venue of the AGM held through video \nconferencing (VC)/ other audio visual means \n(OAV M)\nAugust 19, 2025   12:00 PMNoGround Floor 12A, 94 Meghdoot, Nehru Place, \nNew Delhi -110019, India\nAugust 28, 2024   12:00 PMYe sGround Floor 12A, 94 Meghdoot, Nehru Place, \nNew Delhi -110019, India\nAugust 30, 2023   04:30 PMYe sGround Floor 12A, 94 Meghdoot, Nehru Place, \nNew Delhi -110019, India\nApart from AGM, no other general meeting was held during the financial year 2025-26. \n173\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: CGR\nCompany Overview\n\nPostal Ballot\nDuring the financial year under review, the Company conducted 2 (two) postal ballots in compliance with \nthe provisions of Sections 108 and 110 and other applicable provisions of the Act, read with rules framed \nthereunder, SEBI Listing Regulations and circulars issued by the MCA and SEBI, and accordingly passed 5 \n(five) special resolutions. The notice of the postal ballots containing the draft resolutions and explanatory \nstatement,  were  e-mailed  to  those  members  whose  names  appear  in  the  register  of  members/  register  of  \nbeneficial owners as received from depositories as on respective cut-off dates and whose e-mail addresses \nwere registered with the Company or registrar to an issue and share transfer agent or depository(ies) or \ndepository participants, followed by newspaper publication post dispatch of such postal ballot notices. The \ndetails of the special resolutions passed through postal ballot are given below: \nS r.    \nNo. \nRes\nolutionDate of \ncompletion \nof dispatch \nof Postal \nBallot Notice\nDate of \npassing of \nresolution\nPerson who \nconducted the \npostal ballot \nexercise\nNo. of votes \npolled\nVotes cast in favourVotes cast against\nNo.  \nof votes\n%No\n.  \nof votes\n%\n1To consider and \napprove a cap of up \nto 49.50% on the \naggregate foreign \nownership\nApril 19,  \n2025\nMay 19, \n2025\nNitesh \nLatwal (COP \nno.:16276), \nPartner, M/s. PI \n& Associates, \nCompany \nSecretaries\n6,96,90,02,528 6,95,87,00,95599.85221,03,01,5730.1478\n2Approval for the \nre-appointment of \nAparna Popat Ved \n(DIN: 08661466) \nas independent \ndirector of the \nCompany and \npayment of \nremuneration\nFebruary 11, \n2026\nMarch 13, \n2026\nNitesh \nLatwal (COP \nno.:16276), \nPartner, M/s. PI \n& Associates, \nCompany \nSecretaries\n7,36,78,20,1477,27,34,50,79998.71929,43,69,3481.2808\n3Approval for the \nre-appointment \nof Kaushik Dutta \n(DIN: 03328890) \nas independent \ndirector of the \nCompany and \npayment of \nremuneration\n7,36,39,55,5515,61,34,66,12576.2290   1,75,04,89,42623.7710\n4Approval for the \nre-appointment \nof Namita Gupta \n(DIN: 07337772) \nas independent \ndirector of the \nCompany and \npayment of \nremuneration\n7,36,78,21,2926,96,61,61,23394.548540,16,60,0595.4515\n5Approval for the \nre-appointment of \nSutapa Banerjee \n(DIN: 02844650) \nas independent \ndirector of the \nCompany and \npayment of \nremuneration\n7,36,78,20,251 7,20,11,76,08797.738216,66,44,1642.2618\nNone of the business(es) is proposed to be transacted by passing of a special resolution through postal ballot.\n174\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: CGR\nCompany Overview\n\n6. Means of communication\nThe Company maintains transparent communication with its shareholders through dedicated channels, including annual \ngeneral meetings, periodic letters, newspaper publications, and investor conferences. These initiatives are designed to \nenhance dialogue, strengthen relationships, and promote long-term sustainable value for all stakeholders. \n   The quarterly financial results, shareholders’ letters, annual and event-based stock exchange filings are publicly \naccessible on the websites of NSE at www.nseindia.com, BSE at www.bseindia.com and website of the Company at \nwww.eternal.com.\n   The \ninformation regarding the availability of financial results, together with QR code and web link for accessing such \nfinancial results, is generally published in Financial Express (English newspaper) circulating substantially in the whole \nof India and in Jansatta (vernacular (Hindi) newspaper) in Delhi.\n   The Company provides quarterly updates to the shareholders/ investors on the business performance and financial \nresults through the shareholders’ letters. The Company also hosts earnings conference calls every quarter to address \ninvestor queries on the Company’s performance and financial results. During the year under review, the Company \nconducted 4 earnings conference calls. Audio recordings and transcripts of these calls are available at Link.\n\n   The Company’s AGM for the financial year ended on March 31, 2025 was conducted through video conferencing. The \ntranscript of the proceedings is available at Link.\n      The Company ’s website contains a dedicated section “Investor Relations”. This section is a comprehensive database \nof information including financial results, shareholders letters, annual reports of the Company, shareholder awareness \nmaterials, etc. in an easily accessible manner. Further, the information in terms of Regulation 46 of the SEBI Listing \nRegulations is also provided under this section available at Link.\n\n   The Company has designated e-mail ID: companysecretary@eternal.com for redressal of investors grievances.\n7. General shareholders’ information\nDate, Time and Venue of \nAnnual General Meeting\nDate: August 26, 2026\nTime: 12:00 P.M. (IST)\nVenue: Meeting through VC/ OAVM\nDeemed Venue: Ground Floor 12A, 94 Meghdoot, Nehru Place,  \nNew Delhi – 110019, India\nFinancial yearApril 1 to March 31\nThere has been no change in the financial year.\nDividend Payment DateNot Applicable\nListingThe Equity Shares are listed on:\na)\n BSE Limited \nPhiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai- 400 001\nb) National Stock Exchange of India Limited\nExchange Plaza, C-1, Block G, Bandra Kurla Complex, Bandra (E),  \nMumbai- 400 051\nISININE758T01015\nCINL93030DL2010PLC198141\nListing FeesAnnual listing fees for the financial year 2025-26 (as applicable) have been \npaid to the Stock Exchanges.\n175\nFinancial StatementsStatutory Reports: CGR\nCompany Overview\n\nRegistrar  to  an  issue  and  share  transfer  \nagent \nMUFG Intime India Private Limited (“R TA”)\n(formerly known as Link Intime India Private Limited) \nAddress: Noble Heights, 1\nst\n Floor, Plot NH 2, \nC-1 Block LSC, Near Savitri Market, \nJanakpuri, New Delhi – 110058\nPhone: 011-49411000\nEmail: investor.helpdesk@in.mpms.mufg.com\nWebsite: https://in.mpms.mufg.com/\nContact Person: Vishal Dixit\nSEBI Registration Number: INR000004058\nShare transfer system\nIn terms of the SEBI Listing Regulation, transfer, \ntransmission  and  transposition  of  securities  shall  \nbe   effected   only   in   dematerialised   form.   The   \nshareholder(s) are though not barred from holding \nshares in physical form. However, they are advised to \nhold shares in dematerialised form.\nFurther,     shareholders     holding     shares     in     \ndematerialised  form  are  requested  to  ensure  that  \ntheir email address, bank account details, and mobile \nnumber are registered / updated with their respective \nDepository Participants.\nShareholders holding shares in physical form and \nwho  have  not  registered  their  email  addresses  are  \nrequested  to  register  their  email  address  alongwith  \nPAN, nomination, contact number, bank account \ndetails, postal address with PIN and specimen \nsignature. Shareholders may contact RTA for support \nat  investor  helpdesk  investor.helpdesk@in.mpms.\nmufg.com or call on Tel no.: 022-49186000.\nShareholding Pattern as on March 31, 2026\nS r. \nNo. \nCategoryNo. of \nshareholders\nNo. of  \nshares held\n% of \nshareholding\n(A)Promoter & Promoter group ---\n(B)Public   \n(B)(1)  Institutions1546   6,61,96,27,46368.60\n(B)(2)  Central Govt./ State Govt. / President of India11,65,7390.00\n(B)(3)   Non-Institutions23,03,3372,57,40,98,97726.67\n Total Public Shareholding (B)=(B)(1) +(B)(2) + (B)(3)23,04,8849,19,38,92,17995.27\n(C)Non - Promoter - Non-Public\n(C)(1)Custodian / DR Holder---\n(C)(2)  Shares held by Emp