1	AI Improvement	ai-improvement	A metric defined as the product of computation, algorithms, and data.	AI Improvement is calculated using the formula: computation x algos x data.	2026-08-26 18:46:45.026988+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:45.026988+05:30
2	Effective Compute	effective-compute	The total usable compute calculated by scaling hardware compute with a software multiplier.	Effective compute = hardware compute x software multiplier.	2026-08-26 18:46:45.03829+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:45.03829+05:30
3	Davidson's Model	davidsons-model	A predictive framework used to forecast AI timelines and AI takeoff speeds.	Davidson's model relies on compute-centric frameworks to analyze AI timelines and takeoff speeds. Resources like takeoffspeeds.com and research on coefficientgiving.org allow users to explore and adjust the underlying framework and output values.	2026-08-26 18:46:45.04062+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:45.04062+05:30
4	AI Timelines	ai-timelines	Probabilistic forecasts measuring when AI milestones will be met, quantified in FLOPS.	AI timelines are measured in FLOPS. Predicted probabilities of reaching key AI milestones are: 10% by 2029, 20% by 2032, 50% by 2043, 80% by 2070, and 90% by 2100.	2026-08-26 18:46:45.043824+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:45.043824+05:30
5	AI Takeoff Speed	ai-takeoff-speed	Predictions detailing the duration required for AI takeoff to occur.	Takeoff speed predictions estimate the following durations: 1% probability of 0.3 years, 10% of 0.8 years, 50% of 1.2 years, and 90% of 12.5 years. Interactive values can be rewritten using takeoffspeeds.com.	2026-08-26 18:46:45.046434+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:45.046434+05:30
6	Dario Amodei	dario-amodei	Dario Amodei is an American AI researcher, entrepreneur, and CEO of Anthropic, which he co-founded in 2021. He previously served as vice president of research at OpenAI and is known for writing extensively on the potential benefits and existential risks of advanced artificial intelligence.	Dario Amodei was born in San Francisco in 1983. He studied physics at Caltech and Stanford before earning a doctorate in biophysics from Princeton University in 2011. He worked at Baidu, Google, and OpenAI before co-founding Anthropic in 2021 alongside his sister Daniela Amodei and other former OpenAI staff due to directional differences. As CEO of Anthropic, Amodei advocates for an 'entente' strategy to maintain democratic leadership in AI and has authored essays such as 'Machines of Loving Grace' and 'The Adolescence of Technology'.	2026-08-26 18:46:50.197978+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:50.197978+05:30
7	Anthropic	anthropic	Anthropic is an American artificial intelligence startup founded in 2021 by Dario Amodei, Daniela Amodei, and other former OpenAI senior members. The company is known for developing the Claude large language model series and placing a heavy emphasis on AI safety.	Founded in 2021, Anthropic was created by former OpenAI employees who left due to directional differences. As of May 2026, the company reached an estimated valuation of $965 billion. Anthropic develops the Claude family of models and incorporates strict safety guardrails against domestic mass surveillance and autonomous weapons usage, which triggered a high-profile legal conflict with the U.S. Department of Defense in 2026.	2026-08-26 18:46:50.201767+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:50.201767+05:30
8	Claude	claude	Claude is a series of large language models developed by Anthropic. It is designed with explicit contractual safety terms restricting its use in domestic surveillance and fully autonomous weaponry.	Claude is Anthropic's flagship large language model series. In 2026, contractual terms prohibiting Claude from being used for mass domestic surveillance or fully autonomous weapons became a focal point of conflict between Anthropic and the U.S. Department of Defense.	2026-08-26 18:46:50.206+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:50.206+05:30
9	Machines of Loving Grace	machines-of-loving-grace	'Machines of Loving Grace' is an October 2024 essay written by Dario Amodei outlining a positive vision for how powerful AI could drastically improve human welfare.	Published by Dario Amodei in October 2024, the essay explores how addressing AI risks could unlock rapid technological progress across biology, neuroscience, economic development, global peace, and quality of life. It also outlines the 'entente' policy strategy, advocating that democratic nations maintain technological lead in AI.	2026-08-26 18:46:50.20927+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:50.20927+05:30
10	The Adolescence of Technology	the-adolescence-of-technology	'The Adolescence of Technology' is a January 2026 essay by Dario Amodei detailing the major categories of risk associated with powerful AI.	In this follow-up essay to 'Machines of Loving Grace', Dario Amodei categorizes five major AI risks: misaligned autonomous systems (engaging in deception and scheming), biological weapons and mass destruction misuse, political power seizure and authoritarian surveillance, economic disruption and mass labor displacement, and unknown long-term societal and human purpose challenges.	2026-08-26 18:46:50.212388+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:50.212388+05:30
11	Entente Strategy	entente-strategy	The Entente Strategy is an AI policy framework proposed by Dario Amodei advocating for democratic military dominance in AI.	Proposed by Dario Amodei, the strategy outlines a coalition of democratic nations utilizing advanced military AI to achieve decisive advantages over geopolitical adversaries, while broadly sharing the technology's benefits with cooperating democratic allies to prevent authoritarian dominance.	2026-08-26 18:46:50.214954+05:30	2026-08-26 18:46:50.214954+05:30
